'''Andrew Hamilton Falloon''' (born 29 August 1983)<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.timarucourier.co.nz/views/opinion-youth-are-doing-incredible-things/ |title=OPINION: Youth are doing incredible things |date=19 July 2018 |work=[[The Timaru Courier]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200130163314/http://www.timarucourier.co.nz/views/opinion-youth-are-doing-incredible-things/|archive-date=30 January 2020}}</ref> is a former New Zealand politician, serving as a [[Member of parliament|Member of Parliament]] in the [[New Zealand House of Representatives|House of Representatives]] for the [[New Zealand National Party|National Party]] from 2017 until his resignation in July 2020.

==Early life==
Falloon was born in [[Ashburton, New Zealand|Ashburton]] in 1983. He received his education at Allenton Primary School before boarding at [[Christchurch Boys’ High School]]. He attended the [[University of Canterbury]] to study political science and economics.<ref name="Stuff political obit">{{cite news |last1=Mohanlall |first1=Samesh |title=National MP for Rangitata had a strong presence in community |url= https://www.stuff.co.nz/timaru-herald/news/300061423/national-mp-for-rangitata-had-a-strong-presence-in-community |accessdate=21 July 2020 |work=[[Stuff (website)|Stuff]] |date=20 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720223629/https://www.stuff.co.nz/timaru-herald/news/300061423/national-mp-for-rangitata-had-a-strong-presence-in-community|archive-date=20 July 2020}}</ref>

==Political career==
At the {{NZ election link year|2005}} and {{NZ election link year|2008}} elections Falloon stood as a list-only candidate for [[ACT New Zealand]].<ref name="2005 successful">{{cite web |title=Party Lists of Successful Registered Parties |url= http://electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_2005/e9/html/e9_part3_1.html |publisher=[[Electoral Commission (New Zealand)|Electoral Commission]] |accessdate=22 September 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200511073715/https://www.electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_2005/e9/html/e9_part3_1.html|archive-date=11 May 2020}}</ref><ref name="2008 successful">{{cite web |title=Party Lists of Successful Registered Parties |url=http://www.electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_2008/e9/html/e9_part3_1.html |publisher=[[Electoral Commission (New Zealand)|Electoral Commission]] |accessdate=24 May 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200205084611/https://electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_2008/e9/html/e9_part3_1.html|archive-date=5 February 2020}}</ref> From 2007, he worked as a researcher at Parliament, before working in the ministerial offices of [[Rodney Hide]], [[Phil Heatley]] and [[Steven Joyce]].<ref name="Stuff political obit" /><ref>{{Cite web|last=|first=|date=14 November 2017|title=Address in Reply--Andrew Falloon|url=https://www.parliament.nz/en/pb/hansard-debates/rhr/document/HansS_20171114_062700000/falloon-andrew|access-date=21 July 2020|website=Hansard}}</ref>

