At the [[2017 New Zealand general election|2017 general election]], Falloon contested the [[New Zealand electorates|electorate]] of {{NZ electorate link|Rangitata}} as a candidate for the National Party. Rangitata had been held by National since the electorate was created in 2008.<ref>{{cite news|last=Hayward|first=Michael|url=http://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/91701602/rangitata-national-party-candidate-to-be-andrew-falloon|title=Rangitata National party candidate to be Andrew Falloon|work=[[Stuff (website)|Stuff]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200205084611/https://electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_2008/e9/html/e9_part3_1.html|archive-date=5 February 2020|url-status=live}}</ref> Falloon won the electorate, defeating Labour candidate [[Jo Luxton]] by 6,331 votes.<ref>{{cite web |title=Rangitata - Official Result 2017 general elections |url=https://www.electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_2017/electorate-details-42.html |publisher=[[Electoral Commission (New Zealand)|Electoral Commission]] |accessdate=20 July 2020 |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200115202341/https://electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_2017/electorate-details-42.html |archivedate=15 January 2020}}</ref> With the National Party in Opposition, Falloon was appointed as the party's spokesperson on South Island regional development during [[Simon Bridges]]' leadership, and spokesperson for biosecurity under the leadership of both [[Todd Muller]] and [[Judith Collins]].<ref name="Stuff political obit" />

In 2020, Falloon voted for the [[Abortion Legislation Act 2020|Abortion Legislation Bill]], which decriminalised abortion.<ref>{{cite web |title=Abortion Legislation Bill — Third Reading |url=https://www.parliament.nz/en/pb/hansard-debates/rhr/combined/HansDeb_20200318_20200318_24 |work=[[Parliamentary Debates (Hansard)]] |publisher=New Zealand Parliament |accessdate=21 July 2020 |language=en}}</ref> He supported the [[End of Life Choice Bill]], which aims to legalise voluntary euthanasia.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Littlewood |first1=Matthew |title=Andrew Falloon, Jo Luxton will vote in favour of End of Life Choice Bill |url=https://www.stuff.co.nz/timaru-herald/news/112435717/andrew-falloon-jo-luxton-will-vote-in-favour-of-end-of-life-choice-bill |accessdate=21 July 2020 |work=[[The Timaru Herald]] |date=4 May 2019 |language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720223954/https://www.stuff.co.nz/timaru-herald/news/112435717/andrew-falloon-jo-luxton-will-vote-in-favour-of-end-of-life-choice-bill|archive-date=20 July 2020}}</ref>

====Resignation====
On 20 July 2020, Falloon announced that he would not seek re-election at the [[2020 New Zealand general election|2020 general election]], citing personal reasons following the suicide of a friend.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12349451 |title=National MP Andrew Falloon quits amid 'significant mental health issues' |date=20 July 2020 |work=[[The New Zealand Herald]] |accessdate=20 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720075633/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12349451|archive-date=20 July 2020}}</ref> It was later reported that he had sent a pornographic image to a 19-year-old female university student.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Johnston|first1=Kirsty|last2=Wade|first2=Amelia|date=20 July 2020|title=National MP Andrew Falloon quits after sending sexual image to female university student|work=[[The New Zealand Herald]]|url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12349504|url-status=live|accessdate=20 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720075927/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12349504|archive-date=20 July 2020}}</ref> The parents of the young woman emailed this information to prime minister [[Jacinda Ardern]]; Ardern's chief of staff notified National Party leader [[Judith Collins]]. Police investigated the matter but decided that sending the image did not meet the threshold for prosecution.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Manch |first1=Thomas |last2=Comer |first2=Rachel |title=National MP Andrew Falloon quits politics, alleged to have sent indecent image to young woman |url=https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/300061190/national-mp-andrew-falloon-quits-politics-alleged-to-have-sent-indecent-image-to-school-girl |accessdate=20 July 2020 |work=Stuff |date=20 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720085828/https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/300061190/national-mp-andrew-falloon-quits-politics-alleged-to-have-sent-indecent-image-to-school-girl|archive-date=20 July 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=National MP Andrew Falloon quits politics amid indecent image allegations |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/421642/national-mp-andrew-falloon-quits-politics-amid-indecent-image-allegations |accessdate=21 July 2020 |work=[[RNZ]] |date=21 July 2020}}</ref> According to ''[[The New Zealand Herald]]'', Falloon claimed that he had left his phone unattended during the party and that one of his acquaintances had sent the image. Despite insisting that he had not sent the message, Falloon reportedly offered his resignation to Collins, which she accepted.<ref>{{cite news |title=More details revealed in National MP Andrew Falloon scandal |url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12349534 |accessdate=20 July 2020 |work=[[The New Zealand Herald]] |date=20 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720090325/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12349534|archive-date=20 July 2020}}</ref>

On 21 July 2020, Falloon resigned as a Member of Parliament effective immediately. His resignation accompanied media reports that he had sent two inappropriate images to two other women. Collins also stated that she "no longer trusted his story" of the incident with the first woman and "had lost confidence in him."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Cooke |first1=Henry |title=Andrew Falloon sent sexually explicit photos to another young woman |url=https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/300061529/andrew-falloon-sent-sexually-explicit-photos-to-another-young-woman |accessdate=20 July 2020 |work=[[Stuff (website)|Stuff]] |date=21 July 2020 |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720222603/https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/300061529/andrew-falloon-sent-sexually-explicit-photos-to-another-young-woman |archivedate=20 July 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12349538 |title=New sex-text claims: National MP Andrew Falloon quits politics immediately; Judith Collins says she 'no longer trusts his story' |date=21 July 2020 |work= [[The New Zealand Herald]] |accessdate=21 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720221402/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12349538|archive-date=20 July 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=O'Brien |first1=Tova |title='Pattern of behaviour' emerging: Further allegations of lewd images sent by disgraced ex-National MP Andrew Falloon |url=https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2020/07/pattern-of-behaviour-emerging-further-allegations-of-lewd-images-sent-by-disgraced-ex-national-mp-andrew-falloon.html |accessdate=20 July 2020 |work=[[Newshub]] |date=20 July 2020 |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720222852/https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2020/07/pattern-of-behaviour-emerging-further-allegations-of-lewd-images-sent-by-disgraced-ex-national-mp-andrew-falloon.html |archivedate=20 July 2020}}</ref> After his resignation a total of “at least five"  women have reported similar behaviour by Falloon.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Small |first1=Zane |title=Another woman complains about former National MP Andrew Falloon |url=https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2020/07/at-least-five-complainants-against-ex-national-mp-andrew-falloon-judith-collins.html |accessdate=23 July 2020 |work=[[Newshub]] |date=23 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200723032557/https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2020/07/at-least-five-complainants-against-ex-national-mp-andrew-falloon-judith-collins.html|archive-date=23 July 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Walls |first1=Jason |title=Andrew Falloon sex-text scandal: A fifth woman comes forward with complaint against disgraced MP |url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12350394 |accessdate=23 July 2020 |work=[[New Zealand Herald]] |date=23 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200723032742/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/news/article.cfm?c_id=1&objectid=12350394|archive-date=23 July 2020}}</ref> In response to complaints that Falloon had sent unsolicited explicit messages to multiple women, the [[New Zealand Police]] launched an investigation into the former National MP,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Manch |first1=Thomas |title=Police launch investigation into former National MP Andrew Falloon after allegations he sent explicit messages to young women |url=https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/122228519/police-launch-investigation-into-former-national-mp-andrew-falloon-after-allegations-he-sent-explicit-messages-to-young-women |accessdate=23 July 2020 |work=[[Stuff (website)|Stuff]] |date=23 July 2020 |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200723032930/https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/122228519/police-launch-investigation-into-former-national-mp-andrew-falloon-after-allegations-he-sent-explicit-messages-to-young-women |archivedate=23 July 2020}}</ref> but at the conclusion of the investigation, Police decided not to press charges against him.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/national/433134/no-charges-against-former-national-mp-andrew-falloon-over-unsolicited-images | title=No charges against former National MP Andrew Falloon over unsolicited images | website=[[Radio New Zealand]] | date=18 December 2020 }}</ref>

